+# A physical companion, or a full Value standing as a place's context,
+# describes the reference it was stored with (lmx_value_cell_fill records it).
+# It qualifies a reference just read from that place only while it records the
+# same reference (a present null is ref 0); otherwise the read is an ordinary
+# typed REF without model, references or referent. The one rule of the
+# walker's value and place loads and of the native typed dereference; a
+# context-only temporary is never passed here.
+fn: lmx_value_loaded_context (@: context c.LmxWalkValue; @: raw void) @: c.LmxWalkValue
+    if: context = 0 || context\present = 0 || context\kind != c.LMX_WALK_VALUE_REFERENCE || context\ref != raw
+        return: 0
+    return: context
+end: lmx_value_loaded_context
+
@@ -476,0 +490,5 @@
+# The physical companion's metadata describes the reference it was stored
+# with: after the write succeeds it records that reference (present, kind,
+# ref; a present null is ref 0), so a later raw write of another reference
+# leaves it describing nothing loaded from the cell. Context 0 still clears
+# the metadata. An owner that is not the companion keeps its own Value.
@@ -489,0 +508,5 @@
